turtle@caen.engin.umich.edu (Matthew M Edwards ) writes:

> 
> I'm having a problem.
> 
> Is there any way to tell nethack that we have a black and white
> monitor?  I've tried fiddling with ansi.sys etc but really don't
> know what I am doing.  

In your NETHACK.CNF file add !color to the OPTIONS line.

This loses the color distinction between types of monsters  (ie your
dog and a jackal) and hallucinating is not as much fun.

I run a mono monitor off of a color card and this works for me.  It's
a bit flaky about what it presents as bold characters, but I think
that is in the TERMCAP.

Hope this helps you.


